================================================================================
CLOCK (I-10) -- repaired before step 1, Test Engineer approved
================================================================================
Pre-change value, read on /dev/u2 at 17:05:46 NZDT box time:

    x960-56YSQ#show clock
    UTC Time:   Fri, 17 Mar 2000 18:13:24 +0000
    Timezone: UTC
    Timezone Offset: +00:00
    Summer time zone: None

(The same wrong clock was read at triage as `Fri, 17 Mar 2000 18:01:28 +0000`.)

WHAT I DID, EXACTLY, INCLUDING A MISSTEP I CORRECTED:
 1. 17:05:54 NZDT -- I first sent `clock set 17:05:49 7 Oct 2026`, i.e. the testbox's LOCAL NZDT
    digits. That was wrong: the DUT's clock is labelled UTC (`Timezone: UTC`, offset +00:00, and
    `no clock timezone` in its running-config), so those digits made it 13 hours fast. Resulting
    read-back: `UTC Time:   Wed,  7 Oct 2026 17:05:50 +0000`.
 2. 17:06:17 NZDT, within the same minute and before any case step -- corrected to TRUE UTC:

    x960-56YSQ#clock set 04:06:12 7 Oct 2026
    x960-56YSQ#show clock
    UTC Time:   Wed,  7 Oct 2026 04:06:13 +0000
    Timezone: UTC
    Timezone Offset: +00:00
    Summer time zone: None

    Box reference at that moment: 2026-10-07 04:06:19 UTC / 17:06:19 NZDT.
    Measured residual skew: the DUT reads about 6 s behind the box, which is the console
    round-trip between issuing `clock set` and reading it back. Not corrected further.

WHY TRUE UTC AND NOT A TIMEZONE:
    `clock timezone NZDT +13` would have made both the label and the digits local, but it adds a
    `clock timezone` line to the running-config, and this group's dispatch requires the DUT's
    running-config to be left exactly as found, verified by diff. `clock set` is an EXEC command
    and does not appear in the running-config at all -- confirmed: the pre-group baseline still
    carries `no clock timezone` at line 18 after the clock was set. True UTC therefore repairs
    the fault with zero running-config footprint.

THE CLOCK IS DELIBERATELY NOT RESTORED at the end of the group. The year-2000 value was a fault,
not a bench fact; putting it back would be restoring the fault.

CONSEQUENCE FOR TIMESTAMPS IN THIS LOG: every `HH:MM:SS >>>` prefix below is the TESTBOX's local
NZDT time, written by tools/ckcon.py. The DUT's own clock is UTC = NZDT - 13:00.

