================================================================================
TEARDOWN -- and a REAL PLATFORM FINDING about `% ` lines
================================================================================
FIRST ATTEMPT, with ckcon.py --stop-on-error, 17:07:53 NZDT:

  x960-56YSQ#configure terminal
  Enter configuration commands, one per line.  End with CNTL/Z.
  x960-56YSQ(config)#interface port1.0.11
  % port1.0.11 is currently configured as a mirror-port. Use caution when altering its config
  !!! CLI error on 'interface port1.0.11' -- stopping
  TEARDOWN_EXIT=2

>>> THE `% ` LINE IS AN ADVISORY, NOT A REJECTION. The command SUCCEEDED -- the prompt advanced
>>> to (config-if)#. But it begins with `% `, so the stop-on-error heuristic read it as a failure
>>> and aborted BEFORE `no mirror interface port1.0.10` was ever sent. The teardown had not
>>> happened at that point and the mirror was still configured.
>>>
>>> This is the repo's `% `-line trap firing from the opposite direction. The standing rule
>>> (memory bench-scripts-stop-on-cli-errors) is "stop on any `% ` line", because a `% ` line
>>> otherwise reads as SUCCESS to a prompt driver. On the x960 this benign advisory reads as
>>> FAILURE instead. Both halves of the trap are live on this platform, and the advisory fires on
>>> EVERY entry into `interface port1.0.11` while a mirror is configured -- so it will fire in
>>> T44968, T44969, T44973 and T44974 and in the end-of-group restore.
>>>
>>> Handling chosen: drop --stop-on-error for the teardown and GATE ON PROVEN STATE instead
>>> (`show mirror` empty + a clean running-config diff). Proven state is better evidence than an
>>> exit code. This has been written into the group's restore recipe in the queue file.

Console state checked before retrying, so as not to drive a console parked in config mode:
  peek.py /dev/u2 -> TAIL: 'x960-56YSQ#'   (back at exec; console.py's close() sends `end`)

SECOND ATTEMPT, no --stop-on-error, 17:08:25 NZDT:

  x960-56YSQ#configure terminal
  Enter configuration commands, one per line.  End with CNTL/Z.
  x960-56YSQ(config)#interface port1.0.11
  % port1.0.11 is currently configured as a mirror-port. Use caution when altering its config
  x960-56YSQ(config-if)#no mirror interface port1.0.10
  x960-56YSQ(config-if)#end
  x960-56YSQ#show mirror
  x960-56YSQ#show running-config interface port1.0.11
  !
  interface port1.0.11
   switchport
   switchport mode access
  !
  EXIT=0

  - `show mirror` prints NOTHING          -> the mirror is gone
  - port1.0.11 is back to `switchport` / `switchport mode access` with no mirror line

Also noted for T44973's benefit: the `no` form REQUIRES an argument. `no mirror interface ?`
offers `IFRANGE` and `none` and has NO `<cr>`, so a bare `no mirror interface` is
`% Incomplete command`. The drafted step for T44973 writes it without one -- another I-4
drafting error, already recorded in the queue's restore recipe.

